{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120080","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120080/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120080/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120080/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120080","id":4612570671,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEu4-Lw","number":120080,"title":"MeshInstance3D with 2+ shapekeys affecting the same verticies leads to wrong normals","user":{"login":"Alexofp","id":14040378,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDQwMzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14040378?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp","html_url":"https://github.com/Alexofp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":410064485,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0MTAwNjQ0ODU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/needs%20testing","name":"needs testing","color":"ffcc44","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-08T11:44:07Z","updated_at":"2026-06-08T21:58:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\nMaster\nv4.7.beta5.official [bbd3f43b5]\nv4.7.beta1.official [1c8cc9e7e]\nv4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta5 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 3GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-6400 CPU @ 2.70GHz (4 threads) - 15.95 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm making a game with character customization (body sliders). I've noticed that I had incorrect shading when combining 2 sliders together. I've tested it and yeah, it seems that if a mesh has 2 (or more) shapekeys affecting the same polygons/verticies, godot will calculate the normals incorrectly, leading to wrong shading\n\n<img alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c76fb7e-7ae7-4cf9-8d55-89670958db04\" />\n\nLeft mesh has 2 shapekeys applied separately. Right one has 1 shapekey applied that is the result of combining the 2 shapekeys in Blender.\n\nIf I re-create the same setup in Blender, it looks correctly there (left mesh has 2 applied shapekeys, right one has 1 applied shapekey that is the merge of both):\n\n<img alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7fb21ead-6b06-4e4b-adee-ea3a2aa59165\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87b56864-ac89-4343-829c-301fc1916970\n\n- Create a mesh with 2 shapekeys\n- Apply them both in Godot\n- Observe incorrect shading\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n(has the .blend file too inside if you need it)\n[shapekeybug_2026-06-08_14-33-16.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28705835/shapekeybug_2026-06-08_14-33-16.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120080/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}